  <!-- ══ Foundations ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="foundations">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">07</span><h2>Foundations</h2></div>
    <p class="sub">The primitives every component composes. This is the part that must not drift.</p>

    <div class="grid g2">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Spacing — 4px base, 8px rhythm</div>
        <div class="bars">
          <div class="bar-row"><span>0.5 · 2px</span><div class="b" style="width:2px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>1 · 4px</span><div class="b" style="width:4px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>1.5 · 6px</span><div class="b" style="width:6px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>2 · 8px</span><div class="b" style="width:8px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>3 · 12px</span><div class="b" style="width:12px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>4 · 16px</span><div class="b" style="width:16px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>5 · 20px</span><div class="b" style="width:20px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>6 · 24px</span><div class="b" style="width:24px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>8 · 32px</span><div class="b" style="width:32px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>12 · 48px</span><div class="b" style="width:48px"></div></div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">
          <strong>Rhythm:</strong> between siblings <code>2 / 3 / 4</code>; between regions <code>6 / 8</code>.
          Mixing the two is what makes dense UIs feel cramped <em>and</em> scattered.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Radius — three names are the contract</div>
        <div class="rgrid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);">
          <div class="rbox" style="border-radius:var(--radius-field);">field · 6px</div>
          <div class="rbox" style="border-radius:var(--radius-box);">box · 8px</div>
          <div class="rbox" style="border-radius:var(--radius-selector);">selector · 12px</div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">
          Inputs · cards, panels, dropdowns, toasts · tabs, nav items, <strong>dialogs</strong>.
          <code>radius.full</code> for pills, avatars, dots. <strong>Never mix radii inside one component.</strong>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g2" style="margin-top:12px;">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Elevation — surface + border, not shadow</div>
        <div class="egrid">
          <div class="elayer e0">0 · flat — canvas / panel</div>
          <div class="elayer e1">1 · raised — card + border.subtle</div>
          <div class="elayer e2">2 · overlay — dropdown, toast + shadow-lg</div>
          <div class="elayer e3">3 · modal — dialog + shadow-2xl + backdrop blur</div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">Dark UIs cannot rely on shadows. No shadow on a flat surface, ever.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Motion</div>
        <table style="margin:0;">
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>instant</code></td><td>0ms — press, toggle</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>fast</code></td><td>150ms ease — hover, focus, colour</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>base</code></td><td>200ms ease — sidebar, tab change</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>slow</code></td><td>300ms ease — modal enter</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>sheet</code></td><td>240ms cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1) — mobile sheets</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">
          Animate <code>transform</code> and <code>opacity</code> only · never loop except an in-progress indicator ·
          respect <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> · no entrance animation on streamed content.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin:24px 0 8px;">z-index ladder — one source of truth</h3>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="zrow"><span class="t">z.base</span><span class="v">0</span><span class="zbar" style="width:2%"></span></div>
      <div class="zrow"><span class="t">z.raised</span><span class="v">10</span><span class="zbar" style="width:5%"></span></div>
      <div class="zrow"><span class="t">z.sticky</span><span class="v">20</span><span class="zbar" style="width:10%"></span></div>
      <div class="zrow"><span class="t">z.tabbar</span><span class="v">30</span><span class="zbar" style="width:15%"></span></div>
      <div class="zrow"><span class="t">z.chrome</span><span class="v">50</span><span class="zbar" style="width:25%"></span></div>
      <div class="zrow"><span class="t">z.backdrop</span><span class="v">100</span><span class="zbar" style="width:50%"></span></div>
      <div class="zrow"><span class="t">z.toast</span><span class="v">130</span><span class="zbar" style="width:65%"></span></div>
      <div class="zrow"><span class="t">z.nav</span><span class="v">150</span><span class="zbar" style="width:75%"></span></div>
      <div class="zrow"><span class="t">z.modal</span><span class="v">160</span><span class="zbar" style="width:80%"></span></div>
      <div class="zrow" style="border-bottom:0;"><span class="t">z.popper</span><span class="v">200</span><span class="zbar" style="width:100%"></span></div>
      <p style="margin:10px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">
        <span class="chip err">Bug to fix</span> The modal currently sits at <code>z-50</code> and paints <em>under</em> the
        mobile nav at <code>z-150</code>. Move it to 160. Toasts stay above modals — a failure inside a dialog must be visible.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin:24px 0 8px;">Layout</h3>
    <div class="grid g2">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Desktop ≥ 1025px · rail 64 / 256px + dockview</div>
        <div class="layout">
          <div class="box rail">rail<br>64</div>
          <div class="box col" style="flex:30">chat 30%</div>
          <div class="box col" style="flex:33">changes 33%</div>
          <div class="box col" style="flex:37">preview 37%</div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin:10px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">Panel minimum 280px. Sash: 4px visual seam, <strong>10px pointer target</strong>. Widths persist in <code>ui.panelWidths</code>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Mobile ≤ 1024px · one column</div>
        <div style="display:flex; gap:12px; align-items:flex-start;">
          <div class="phone">
            <div class="top">top bar · 56px</div>
            <div class="mid">content · 16px side padding</div>
            <div class="bot"><span class="on">Home</span><span>Chats</span><span>Tasks</span><span>More</span></div>
          </div>
          <div style="font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">
            <p style="margin:0 0 8px;">Tab bar 60px + <code>safe-area-inset-bottom</code>.</p>
            <p style="margin:0 0 8px;">No side-by-side panes — use a <strong>sheet</strong> or a <strong>route</strong>.</p>
            <p style="margin:0;">Touch targets ≥ <strong>44×44px</strong>, 8px minimum gap. Modal becomes <code>fullscreen</code> (100dvh, radius 0).</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tbl-wrap" style="margin-top:12px;">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Breakpoint</th><th>Range</th><th>Shell</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>mobile</td><td>0 – 640px</td><td>Mobile shell</td></tr>
          <tr><td>tablet</td><td>641 – 1024px</td><td><strong>Mobile shell</strong> (open decision — see §15)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>desktop</td><td>1025 – 1535px</td><td>Desktop rail 64px + dockview</td></tr>
          <tr><td>wide</td><td>≥ 1536px</td><td>Desktop, three panes visible</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="ramp-note"><span class="chip warn">Gotcha</span> The ≤1024px boundary is decided in <strong>JS</strong>
      (<code>store/ui.js → handleResize</code>), not by a CSS media query. <code>md:</code>/<code>lg:</code> utilities
      cannot compensate — verify every layout with <code>isMobile</code> both true and false.</p>
  </section>

