  <!-- ══ Patterns ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="patterns">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">09</span><h2>Patterns &amp; states</h2></div>
    <p class="sub">The states that are usually forgotten. Every list, board, table, panel and route
      needs all of them designed.</p>

    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>State</th><th>What to design</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Loading</td><td>Skeleton with the real layout (5 rows, real column widths). Never a full-page spinner for a section refresh. &lt; 300ms: show nothing.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Empty (first use)</td><td>One sentence of what this is + one primary action. No illustration.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Empty (filtered)</td><td>"No results for <code>auth</code>" + <code>Clear filters</code>. Never the first-use text.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Error</td><td>Inline block with retry; the panel stays open. Full-page error only when the route cannot render.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Streaming / running</td><td>Persistent step trace + elapsed + cancel. Composer never scrolls away.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Permission denied</td><td>Explanation + the action that requests access.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Offline / disconnected</td><td>Sidebar footer shows <code>offline</code>; banner when actions are blocked.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g3">
      <div class="demo">
        <div class="demo-label">Skeleton loading</div>
        <div style="display:grid; gap:8px;">
          <div class="bar-mock" style="height:10px; width:70%; background:color-mix(in oklab, var(--fg) 10%, transparent); border-radius:3px;"></div>
          <div class="bar-mock" style="height:10px; width:95%; background:color-mix(in oklab, var(--fg) 7%, transparent); border-radius:3px;"></div>
          <div class="bar-mock" style="height:10px; width:84%; background:color-mix(in oklab, var(--fg) 7%, transparent); border-radius:3px;"></div>
          <div class="bar-mock" style="height:10px; width:60%; background:color-mix(in oklab, var(--fg) 7%, transparent); border-radius:3px;"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="demo">
        <div class="demo-label">Inline error with recovery</div>
        <div style="display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:8px; padding:10px; border-radius:6px; background:color-mix(in oklab, var(--error) 10%, transparent); border:1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--error) 28%, transparent);">
          <span style="color:var(--error);">✕</span>
          <div>
            <div style="font-size:13px; font-weight:600;">Couldn't reach the API.</div>
            <div style="font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">Check the container is running, then retry.</div>
            <div style="display:flex; gap:6px; margin-top:8px;"><button class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm">Retry</button><button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm">View logs</button></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="demo">
        <div class="demo-label">Progress &gt; 10s (agent work)</div>
        <div style="font-size:13px; color:var(--fg-2);">
          <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; margin-bottom:6px;"><span>Running tests… 3 of 12</span><span class="mono">1m 08s</span></div>
          <div style="height:4px; border-radius:2px; background:color-mix(in oklab, var(--fg) 10%, transparent); overflow:hidden;"><div style="width:25%; height:100%; background:var(--primary);"></div></div>
          <div style="margin-top:8px;"><button class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm">Cancel run</button></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ IA ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="ia">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Information architecture</h2></div>
    <p class="sub">codx-junior does not have pages. It has <strong>apps</strong> that open in two ways:
      a dockview <em>panel</em> on desktop, a router <em>route</em> on mobile. Design for both, always.</p>

    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:16px; font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:12px; line-height:22px; overflow-x:auto;">
      <div style="color:var(--fg-4);">// the only navigation primitive</div>
      <div>user action → <span style="color:var(--primary-fg)">openApp(key, payload)</span> <span style="color:var(--fg-4)">// reads config/apps.js</span></div>
      <div>&nbsp;&nbsp;├─ !isMobile → <strong>dockview PANEL</strong> <span style="color:var(--fg-4)">(multi-instance by params)</span></div>
      <div>&nbsp;&nbsp;└─&nbsp;&nbsp;isMobile → <strong>ROUTE</strong> <span style="color:var(--fg-4)">(params in the URL)</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g2" style="margin-bottom:12px;">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Four shells</div>
        <table style="margin:0;">
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Desktop</td><td>64/256px rail + dockview + status/toast</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Mobile ≤1024px</td><td>56px top bar + content + 60px tab bar</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Company</td><td>Own tab bar: Company · Ask · Add person · New team · More</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Solopreneur</td><td>Full-screen route, no codx-junior chrome</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Naming conventions</div>
        <table style="margin:0;">
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>App titles</td><td>Title Case · <code>Task Manager</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Panel titles</td><td>Instance-qualified · <code>Tasks — Sprint 12</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Routes</td><td>kebab-case · <code>/git-view</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Profiles</td><td><code>snake_case</code> id, Title Case in prose</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Machine values</td><td>mono, unchanged</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin:20px 0 8px;">The app catalogue — grouped the way users think</h3>
    <div class="grid g2">
      <div class="demo"><div class="demo-label">Work</div><p style="margin:0; font-size:13px; color:var(--fg-2);">Home · Chats · New chat · Task Manager · Planning · Company · Management · Projects · Harness</p></div>
      <div class="demo"><div class="demo-label">People</div><p style="margin:0; font-size:13px; color:var(--fg-2);">Messenger · Meet · Team · Team channel</p></div>
      <div class="demo"><div class="demo-label">Build</div><p style="margin:0; font-size:13px; color:var(--fg-2);">Files · File viewer · Git · Workspaces · Browsers · Infrastructure · Wiki · Docs · Knowledge</p></div>
      <div class="demo"><div class="demo-label">Insights</div><p style="margin:0; font-size:13px; color:var(--fg-2);">Analytics · Metrics · API monitoring · Chat logs · Decision logs · Logs</p></div>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin:20px 0 8px;">The five flows that matter</h3>
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th style="width:190px;">Flow</th><th>Design requirement</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>F1</strong> Ask, watch it happen</td><td>Step trace always visible while running; cost and time accrue in place; composer never scrolls away; a finished run collapses to a summary.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>F2</strong> Track the work</td><td>Card = task + conversation + artifacts. Dragging must not lose scroll or selection. Board, Planning, Sprint and Table are views of the same tasks.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>F3</strong> Review a change</td><td>Diff typography is non-negotiable (mono, fixed line-height, tab-size 2). Three panes on desktop, three routes on mobile. Risk summary on top.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>F4</strong> Hand over to a machine session</td><td>The live view is the hero; the control lease (who is driving) is always visible; the handover banner is the only switch.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>F5</strong> Understand cost &amp; health</td><td>One time-window control reused everywhere; every number has a unit and a comparison; partial-data states designed.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="card" style="border-left:3px solid var(--warning);">
      <div class="demo-label">Design debt</div>
      <p style="margin:0; font-size:13px; color:var(--fg-2);">Desktop hides apps behind <code>WindowsMenu</code>, mobile behind
        <em>More</em> — two mental models for one catalogue. Target: <strong>one "Everything" launcher</strong> for both shells,
        same grouping and search (the mobile <code>MOBILE_APP_GROUPS</code> already models it — promote it).</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ A11y ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="a11y">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Accessibility</h2><span class="chip">WCAG 2.2 AA</span></div>
    <p class="sub">Not a phase — a release condition. Contrast, keyboard and focus are the three that
      regress silently, so they are the three that get checked every time.</p>

    <div class="grid g2">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Current status</div>
        <div class="a11y">
          <div class="item"><span class="chip err">✕</span><span>Magenta text on dark canvas — 3.1:1 (needs 4.5)</span></div>
          <div class="item"><span class="chip err">✕</span><span>Modal at <code>z-50</code> paints under the mobile nav</span></div>
          <div class="item"><span class="chip err">✕</span><span>No focus trap in <code>Modal.vue</code>; focus not restored</span></div>
          <div class="item"><span class="chip warn">△</span><span>Collapsed rail relies on <code>title</code>, not real tooltips</span></div>
          <div class="item"><span class="chip warn">△</span><span>Headings styled by size, not by document outline</span></div>
          <div class="item"><span class="chip ok">✓</span><span>Decorative icons carry <code>aria-hidden</code> (MobileTabBar)</span></div>
          <div class="item"><span class="chip ok">✓</span><span>Status colour always paired with a word</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Keyboard contract</div>
        <table style="margin:0;">
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><span class="kbd">Tab</span> / <span class="kbd">Shift+Tab</span></td><td>Move through focusables in DOM order</td></tr>
            <tr><td><span class="kbd">Esc</span></td><td>Close the topmost overlay (modal, sheet, dropdown)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><span class="kbd">←</span> <span class="kbd">→</span> <span class="kbd">Home</span> <span class="kbd">End</span></td><td>Tabs, segmented controls, roving tabindex</td></tr>
            <tr><td><span class="kbd">Enter</span> / <span class="kbd">Space</span></td><td>Activate the focused control</td></tr>
            <tr><td><span class="kbd">⌘/Ctrl+Enter</span></td><td>Send the chat message</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p style="margin:10px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">
          <strong>Focus contract:</strong> <code>outline: 2px solid var(--color-primary)</code>, offset 2px — or
          <code>ring-2 ring-primary/50</code>. Visible on both themes, never removed, never only on <code>:hover</code>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin:20px 0 8px;">Touch &amp; motion</h3>
    <div class="grid g3">
      <div class="demo"><div class="demo-label">Touch</div><p style="margin:0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">Targets ≥ 44×44px, 8px gaps, row actions always visible on touch (not hover-only).</p></div>
      <div class="demo"><div class="demo-label">Motion</div><p style="margin:0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);"><code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> disables every transition group, not only the mobile shell.</p></div>
      <div class="demo"><div class="demo-label">Zoom</div><p style="margin:0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">200% zoom without horizontal loss; text stays ≥ 14px in dense surfaces.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ Code ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="code">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Implement it</h2></div>
    <p class="sub">Five concrete steps, in order. Nothing here needs design input — it is safe to start today.</p>

    <div class="codeblock">
      <div class="bar"><span class="file">client/src/assets/tokens.css — generated from design/tokens/design-tokens.json</span>
      <button class="copybtn" data-copy=":root {
  /* brand */
  --color-brand-400: oklch(72% 0.19 340);   /* #FF69B4 — text on dark */
  --color-brand-600: oklch(56% 0.28 330);   /* #CC0099 — the brand */
  --color-brand-800: oklch(38% 0.19 330);
  /* secondary */
  --color-secondary-600: oklch(45% 0.24 330); /* #8F008F — fill only */
  /* radius: three names are the contract */
  --radius-field: 0.375rem;
  --radius-box: 0.5rem;
  --radius-selector: 0.75rem;
  /* type */
  --font-sans: system-ui, -apple-system, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Arial, sans-serif;
  --font-mono: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, &quot;SF Mono&quot;, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
}">Copy</button></div>
      <pre><code><span class="k">:root</span> {
  <span class="c">/* brand */</span>
  --color-brand-400: <span class="s">oklch(72% 0.19 340)</span>;   <span class="c">/* #FF69B4 — text on dark */</span>
  --color-brand-600: <span class="s">oklch(56% 0.28 330)</span>;   <span class="c">/* #CC0099 — the brand */</span>
  --color-brand-800: <span class="s">oklch(38% 0.19 330)</span>;
  <span class="c">/* secondary */</span>
  --color-secondary-600: <span class="s">oklch(45% 0.24 330)</span>; <span class="c">/* #8F008F — fill only */</span>
  <span class="c">/* radius: three names are the contract */</span>
  --radius-field: <span class="s">0.375rem</span>;
  --radius-box: <span class="s">0.5rem</span>;
  --radius-selector: <span class="s">0.75rem</span>;
  <span class="c">/* type */</span>
  --font-sans: <span class="s">system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif</span>;
  --font-mono: <span class="s">ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace</span>;
}</code></pre>
    </div>

    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th style="width:44px;">#</th><th>Step</th><th style="width:170px;">Why / files</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>1</td><td>Delete dead brand code: <code>daisy-override.css</code>, <code>assets/themes/*.css</code>, <code>src/assets/logo.svg</code></td><td>598 lines re-tinting 35 themes that never load; the SVG is the Vue logo</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2</td><td>Fix the broken <code>@font-face</code> in <code>main.css</code> and adopt the mono stack</td><td>Real rendering bug — the face never loads</td></tr>
          <tr><td>3</td><td>Emit <code>tokens.css</code>; register exactly two daisyUI themes; restrict <code>ThemeSelector</code></td><td>35 themes → 2; per-theme primary (light <code>#CC0099</code>, dark <code>oklch(65% .32 320)</code>)</td></tr>
          <tr><td>4</td><td>CI guard: no raw hex outside <code>tokens.css</code></td><td>Stops the drift at the source</td></tr>
          <tr><td>5</td><td>Modal: focus trap, <code>z-160</code>, <code>radius.modal</code></td><td>Accessibility + the layering bug</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="codeblock">
      <div class="bar"><span class="file">CI check — copy into the pipeline</span>
      <button class="copybtn" data-copy="rg -n '#[0-9a-fA-F]{6}' client/src --glob '!**/tokens.css' --glob '!**/fontawesome*/**'">Copy</button></div>
      <pre><code>rg -n <span class="s">'#[0-9a-fA-F]{6}'</span> client/src --glob <span class="s">'!**/tokens.css'</span> --glob <span class="s">'!**/fontawesome*/**'</span></code></pre>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
      <div class="demo-label">PR checklist — paste into the template</div>
      <ul style="margin:0; font-size:13px; color:var(--fg-2); columns: 2; column-gap: 32px;">
        <li>Tokens only (no raw hex, no arbitrary px, no new radius)</li>
        <li>Both themes checked (dark + light)</li>
        <li>390 / 768 / 1024 / 1280 / 1920 px</li>
        <li><code>isMobile</code> true <em>and</em> false</li>
        <li>All six states defined</li>
        <li>Keyboard reachable, focus visible, Esc closes</li>
        <li>Contrast verified (text, borders, icons, ring)</li>
        <li>Colour never the only meaning carrier</li>
        <li>Touch targets ≥ 44px</li>
        <li>Copy follows voice &amp; tone</li>
        <li>Empty / filtered / loading / error designed</li>
        <li>One icon set, <code>aria-hidden</code> / <code>aria-label</code></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ Do / Don't ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="dodont">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Do / Don't</h2></div>
    <p class="sub">The seven mistakes that were actually found in the codebase, as pairs.</p>

    <div class="pair">
      <div class="do"><div class="h">✓ Do</div><div class="body">Use <code>#CC0099</code> for magenta and <code>#FF69B4</code> for magenta <em>text</em> on dark. One value per role.</div></div>
      <div class="dont"><div class="h">✕ Don't</div><div class="body">Introduce <code>#CC049C</code> (a 3/255 near-miss) or resurrect <code>#6366F1</code> indigo. Three palettes is how "brand colour" stops being a value.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pair">
      <div class="do"><div class="h">✓ Do</div><div class="body">Keep <code>radius.field</code> / <code>radius.box</code> / <code>radius.selector</code>. One radius per component.</div></div>
      <div class="dont"><div class="h">✕ Don't</div><div class="body">Mix 12px body + 8px header + pill button in one card. It reads as three objects.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pair">
      <div class="do"><div class="h">✓ Do</div><div class="body">Show every number with a unit and, in a column, tabular figures. <code>12.4k tokens</code> · <code>$0.42</code> · <code>2m 12s</code>.</div></div>
      <div class="dont"><div class="h">✕ Don't</div><div class="body">Write <code>12.4k</code>, <code>0.42</code>, <code>132 seconds</code> — or a UI string with no unit at all.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pair">
      <div class="do"><div class="h">✓ Do</div><div class="body">Pair status colour with a word or icon: <span class="badge success"><span class="dot on"></span>online</span></div></div>
      <div class="dont"><div class="h">✕ Don't</div><div class="body">Use a bare green dot, a red border, or a magenta element to mean "error".</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pair">
      <div class="do"><div class="h">✓ Do</div><div class="body">Use <code>fa-solid</code> for UI chrome, <code>fa-regular</code> for soft nav and empty states — one set per surface.</div></div>
      <div class="dont"><div class="h">✕ Don't</div><div class="body">Mix Font Awesome and Iconify in one view; use emoji as UI icons; reuse <code>fa-comments</code> for both Chat and Messenger.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pair">
      <div class="do"><div class="h">✓ Do</div><div class="body">Design the panel <em>and</em> the route; give multi-instance apps a qualified title (<code>Tasks — Sprint 12</code>).</div></div>
      <div class="dont"><div class="h">✕ Don't</div><div class="body">Ship a screen that only works with a 256px sidebar next to it — on mobile it becomes a headless page.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pair" style="margin-bottom:0;">
      <div class="do"><div class="h">✓ Do</div><div class="body">Write the error: <em>what failed · why · what to do next</em>, then keep the panel open.</div></div>
      <div class="dont"><div class="h">✕ Don't</div><div class="body">"Something went wrong." · "Error: [object Object]" · "Oops! 😢"</div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ Roadmap ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="roadmap">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Roadmap</h2></div>
    <p class="sub">Sequenced so each phase removes a class of future inconsistency. S ≤ 2 days · M ≤ 1 week · L &gt; 1 week (one frontend).</p>
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th style="width:52px;">Phase</th><th>Content</th><th style="width:96px;">Effort</th><th style="width:110px;">Status</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>0</td><td>Stop the drift: delete dead brand CSS + Vue logo, fix <code>@font-face</code>, retire indigo, CI hex guard</td><td>≈3 days</td><td><span class="chip ok">ready</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>1</td><td>Tokens live: <code>tokens.css</code>, two daisyUI themes, per-theme primary, restrict the theme selector</td><td>≈1 week</td><td><span class="chip ok">ready</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>2</td><td>Corporate image: vector logo + variants, favicon/PWA/OG, sidebar lockup, re-shoot screenshots, deck templates</td><td>≈2 weeks</td><td><span class="chip warn">blocked</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>3</td><td>Components: modal focus trap + <code>z-160</code>, shared <code>DataTable</code>, button/input/badge recipes, handover banner, chat spec, empty states, local avatars</td><td>≈3 weeks</td><td><span class="chip">queued</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>4</td><td>UX debt: one "Everything" launcher for both shells, one navigation model, keyboard operation for boards, <code>aria-live</code> streaming</td><td>≈2 weeks</td><td><span class="chip">queued</span></td></tr>
          <tr><td>5</td><td>Governance: design review in the PR template, published accessibility statement, published design system, quarterly brand audit</td><td>ongoing</td><td><span class="chip">queued</span></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin:20px 0 8px;">Metrics that tell you it is working</h3>
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Baseline</th><th>Target</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Distinct brand palettes in the repo</td><td>3</td><td><strong>1</strong></td></tr>
          <tr><td>daisyUI themes offered to users</td><td>35</td><td><strong>2</strong></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Raw hex literals outside <code>tokens.css</code></td><td>many</td><td><strong>0</strong></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Contrast failures on primary screens</td><td>≥ 1</td><td><strong>0</strong></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Lighthouse accessibility (Home / Chat / Board)</td><td>unknown</td><td><strong>≥ 90</strong></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin:20px 0 8px;">Open decisions — they need a human, not more analysis</h3>
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th style="width:40px;">#</th><th>Decision</th><th>Blocks</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>1</td><td>Logo: glyph + wordmark, <em>or</em> typographic-only (magenta hyphen as the mark)?</td><td>All of Phase 2</td></tr>
          <tr><td>2</td><td>Adopt a licensed webfont for marketing/headings, or stay 100% system?</td><td>Typography §2</td></tr>
          <tr><td>3</td><td>Tablets (641–1024px): keep the mobile shell, or build a compact desktop?</td><td>IA + layout rules</td></tr>
          <tr><td>4</td><td>Is <code>codx-junior-light</code> a supported theme or a convenience?</td><td>Colour work, QA matrix</td></tr>
          <tr><td>5</td><td>Do profiles get individual avatars as part of the brand system?</td><td>Asset set</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

