  <section id="cover" class="cover">
    <div class="kicker">Corporate image · design playbook</div>
    <h1>The codx-junior design playbook</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      One page a developer can read before writing UI code. Every value here is derived
      from the shipped product (<code>client/</code>) and from the decisions in
      <code>design/</code>. The specimens on this page are rendered with the real
      tokens — if it looks wrong here, it will look wrong in the app.
    </p>
    <div class="meta">
      <span class="chip brand">v0.1 · proposal</span>
      <span class="chip">2 themes · 1 brand</span>
      <span class="chip">WCAG 2.2 AA target</span>
      <span class="chip warn">Not yet wired into <code>client/</code></span>
    </div>
    <div class="card" style="margin-top:24px; border-left:3px solid var(--primary);">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom:6px;">Read this first</h3>
      <p style="margin:0; color:var(--fg-2);">
        The app currently runs on stock daisyUI themes: the brand CSS
        (<code>daisy-override.css</code>, <code>assets/themes/*.css</code>) is
        <strong>not imported by any entry point</strong>. This playbook is the target state, and
        the tokens in it are authoritative. If a component disagrees with a token, the
        component is the bug.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ 10 rules ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="rules">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">01</span><h2>The 10 rules</h2></div>
    <p class="sub">If you remember nothing else, remember these. They are the decisions that
      prevented 90% of the inconsistency found in the audit.</p>
    <div class="rules">
      <div class="rule"><span class="n">1</span><div><b>Two themes, one brand</b><span>Dark is default, light is supported. Never add a third palette or a "temporary" accent.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><span class="n">2</span><div><b>Magenta text on dark is pink</b><span><code>#CC0099</code> is a fill (white text, 4.8:1). As <em>text</em> on dark use <code>#FF69B4</code> (5.5:1).</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><span class="n">3</span><div><b>Tokens only</b><span>No raw hex, no arbitrary px, no new radius outside <code>tokens.css</code>.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><span class="n">4</span><div><b>Magenta ≤ 10% of pixels</b><span>An accent is an accent. A screen that is mostly magenta has lost its hierarchy.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><span class="n">5</span><div><b>Two voices only</b><span>Interface sans, and mono for anything you could paste into a terminal. No third family.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><span class="n">6</span><div><b>Compact by default</b><span>13–14px text, 12px row padding, 36px rows. There is no "comfortable" mode.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><span class="n">7</span><div><b>Elevation = surface + border</b><span>Shadows only for overlay and modal. Never a shadow on a flat surface.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><span class="n">8</span><div><b>Six states, always</b><span>default · hover · focus-visible · active · disabled · loading. All six, every component.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><span class="n">9</span><div><b>Colour is never the only meaning</b><span>Every status colour is paired with a word or an icon.</span></div></div>
      <div class="rule"><span class="n">10</span><div><b>Panel and route, both</b><span>Same app renders in dockview (desktop) and as a full route (mobile). Check <code>isMobile</code> true and false.</span></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ Brand ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="brand">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">02</span><h2>What codx-junior is</h2></div>
    <p class="sub">The product is an AI teammate that runs inside your project — chats, runs,
      boards, workspaces, browsers — on one screen, with you watching. The design has to make
      a machine's work legible and reversible.</p>

    <div class="grid g2" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Positioning</div>
        <p style="margin:0; font-size:16px; line-height:26px;">
          <strong>codx-junior turns a project into a place where work happens.</strong>
          Not a chat window bolted onto an IDE, not a dashboard about work — the
          workbench itself.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Who it is for</div>
        <ul style="margin:0; color:var(--fg-2); font-size:13px;">
          <li><strong>The solo builder</strong> who wants a team, not a tool.</li>
          <li><strong>The tech lead</strong> who must see what the AI did and why.</li>
          <li><strong>The team</strong> mixing humans and profiles behind one board.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin-bottom:10px;">Five personality traits</h3>
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th style="width:130px;">Trait</th><th>It means</th><th>In the UI</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Composed</td><td>Never shouts, never panics</td><td>No exclamation marks, no red decoration, calm empty states</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Precise</td><td>Numbers and names, not adjectives</td><td>Paths, durations, token counts, model ids — always with units</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Transparent</td><td>The work is visible while it runs</td><td>Persistent step trace, cost accrues in place, diffs inline</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Reversible</td><td>Everything can be undone or taken over</td><td>Cancel, retry, branch, restore; handover banner for humans</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Warm, not cute</td><td>Personality lives in copy, not mascots</td><td>No illustrations in-product, no emoji icons, one human moment on the landing page</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="pair">
      <div class="do"><div class="h">✓ Do</div><div class="body">"Running tests… 3 of 12" · "Merged" · "Couldn't reach the API. Check the container, then retry."</div></div>
      <div class="dont"><div class="h">✕ Don't</div><div class="body">"Oops! Something went wrong 😢" · "Successfully saved!" · "Unexpected error occurred."</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="card" style="margin-top:20px; display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr)); gap:20px; align-items:center;">
      <figure class="shot">
        <img src="../resources/me-and-codx-junior.png"
             alt="Photograph of two people standing side by side in an office"
             width="260" height="259">
      </figure>
      <div>
        <div class="demo-label">The one human moment</div>
        <p style="margin:0 0 8px; color:var(--fg-2);">
          codx-junior is made by people and used by people sitting next to a machine. The brand allows
          <strong>exactly one photograph per surface</strong> — real room, real people, no stock, no mascot —
          and this is the supplied reference: <code>design/resources/me-and-codx-junior.png</code>
          (1028 × 1024, opaque PNG).
        </p>
        <ul style="margin:0; color:var(--fg-2); font-size:13px;">
          <li>Landing page, About, talks and deck credit slides — <strong>never</strong> inside the product UI.</li>
          <li>Not an avatar, not a profile picture, not a testimonial.</li>
          <li>A signed model release is required before external or paid use.</li>
          <li>Never crop a person out to fit a banner, never filter or AI-retouch it.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ Logo ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="logo">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">03</span><h2>Logo system</h2><span class="chip warn">Gap: raster only · no vector master</span></div>
    <p class="sub">The authentic artwork is <code>design/resources/logo.png</code>: a folded ribbon whose bands
      interlock at 90° and 45° around a hollow, fully transparent centre, filled with a magenta → violet
      gradient. It is a <strong>single 267 × 266 raster file</strong> — there is no vector master, and
      <code>src/assets/logo.svg</code> in the app is still the <strong>Vue.js logo</strong>. Every specimen on this
      page renders that exact file, never a redraw.</p>

    <div class="grid g3" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
      <div class="demo" style="display:grid; place-items:center; gap:10px; padding:24px;">
        <div class="demo-label" style="margin:0;">Glyph · transparent</div>
        <img src="../resources/logo.png" alt="codx-junior folded-ribbon logo mark" width="72" height="72">
        <span class="mono" style="color:var(--fg-3);">min 16px</span>
      </div>
      <div class="demo" style="padding:24px;">
        <div class="demo-label">Horizontal lockup · min 88px</div>
        <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:12px;">
          <img src="../resources/logo.png" alt="" width="34" height="34">
          <span style="font-size:24px; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:-.01em;">codx<span style="color:var(--primary-fg)">-</span>junior</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="demo" style="padding:24px; display:grid; place-items:center; gap:8px;">
        <div class="demo-label" style="margin:0;">Stacked · min 64px</div>
        <img src="../resources/logo.png" alt="" width="30" height="30">
        <span style="font-size:13px; font-weight:600;">codx<span style="color:var(--primary-fg)">-</span>junior</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin:24px 0 8px;">Four mandatory colour variants</h3>
    <div class="grid g4" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
      <div class="demo" style="background:#1F2937; border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.1);">
        <div class="demo-label" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,.45);">Primary / dark</div>
        <img src="../resources/logo.png" alt="" width="28" height="28">
        <div style="color:#fff; font-weight:600; font-size:12px; margin-top:6px;">codx<span style="color:#FF69B4">-</span>junior</div>
      </div>
      <div class="demo" style="background:#fff; border-color:#E2E2EA;">
        <div class="demo-label" style="color:#9CA3AF;">Monochrome dark</div>
        <span class="mark mark-28" style="color:#111827" role="img" aria-label="codx-junior mark, monochrome black"></span>
        <div style="color:#111827; font-weight:600; font-size:12px; margin-top:6px;">codx-junior</div>
      </div>
      <div class="demo" style="background:#111827; border-color:#111827;">
        <div class="demo-label" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,.4);">Monochrome light</div>
        <span class="mark mark-28" style="color:#FFFFFF" role="img" aria-label="codx-junior mark, monochrome white"></span>
        <div style="color:#fff; font-weight:600; font-size:12px; margin-top:6px;">codx-junior</div>
      </div>
      <div class="demo" style="background:#fff; border-color:#E2E2EA;">
        <div class="demo-label" style="color:#9CA3AF;">Single colour</div>
        <span class="mark mark-28" style="color:#CC0099" role="img" aria-label="codx-junior mark, single magenta"></span>
        <div style="color:#CC0099; font-weight:600; font-size:12px; margin-top:6px;">codx-junior</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g2">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Construction rules</div>
        <table style="margin:0;">
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Glyph geometry</td><td>Interlocking folded ribbon; constant band width; every joint 90° or 45°; hollow, transparent centre</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Gradient</td><td>Ribbon only, magenta → violet (sampled ≈ <code>#CC0099 → #800080</code>); never reversed, never on the wordmark</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Gap glyph → wordmark</td><td>0.5 × glyph width</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Clear space</td><td>≥ 0.5 × glyph height, never less than the height of the <code>c</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Minimum sizes</td><td>Glyph 16px · horizontal 88px · stacked 64px</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Monochrome variants</td><td>Shown above with a CSS mask of the same PNG — a demo trick; production needs real one-colour paths</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Master file today</td><td><code>design/resources/logo.png</code> — 267 × 266 px, alpha, <strong>no vector source</strong> ⚠️</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Hard "no"</div>
        <ul style="margin:0; color:var(--fg-2); font-size:13px;">
          <li>Stretch, squash, rotate, outline or drop-shadow</li>
          <li>Recolour outside the four variants (no teal, no indigo)</li>
          <li>Wordmark in caps, in another font, or with a space (<code>codx junior</code>)</li>
          <li>The lockup inside a rounded card or circle — except the app icon</li>
          <li>Animate the logo on every load (one landing-page reveal only)</li>
          <li>Use the logo as a bullet, an avatar or a spinner</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ Colour ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="colour">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">04</span><h2>Colour</h2></div>
    <p class="sub">One brand hue, one neutral ramp with a blue-slate bias (so magenta does not
      vibrate), four semantics. Click any swatch to copy its hex.</p>

    <h3 style="margin-bottom:8px;">Magenta — the signature</h3>
    <div class="ramp">
      <button class="swatch dark-txt" style="background:#FFF0FA" data-copy="#FFF0FA"><span class="step">50</span><span>#FFF0FA</span></button>
      <button class="swatch dark-txt" style="background:#FFD6F0" data-copy="#FFD6F0"><span class="step">100</span><span>#FFD6F0</span></button>
      <button class="swatch dark-txt" style="background:#FFAEE0" data-copy="#FFAEE0"><span class="step">200</span><span>#FFAEE0</span></button>
      <button class="swatch dark-txt" style="background:#FF80CE" data-copy="#FF80CE"><span class="step">300</span><span>#FF80CE</span></button>
      <button class="swatch dark-txt" style="background:#FF69B4" data-copy="#FF69B4"><span class="step">400</span><span>#FF69B4</span></button>
      <button class="swatch light-txt" style="background:#F530A8" data-copy="#F530A8"><span class="step">500</span><span>#F530A8</span></button>
      <button class="swatch light-txt" style="background:#CC0099" data-copy="#CC0099"><span class="step">600</span><span>#CC0099</span></button>
      <button class="swatch light-txt" style="background:#A3007A" data-copy="#A3007A"><span class="step">700</span><span>#A3007A</span></button>
      <button class="swatch light-txt" style="background:#7A005B" data-copy="#7A005B"><span class="step">800</span><span>#7A005B</span></button>
      <button class="swatch light-txt" style="background:#4D0039" data-copy="#4D0039"><span class="step">900</span><span>#4D0039</span></button>
    </div>
    <p class="ramp-note"><strong>600 = #CC0099 is <em>the</em> brand colour.</strong> 400 (#FF69B4) is the
      dark-mode text colour. 900 is the tinted dark background. Retired: <code>#CC049C</code> (a 3/255
      near-miss from dead CSS) and <code>#6366F1</code> indigo (old Designer profile).</p>

    <h3 style="margin-bottom:8px;">Purple — secondary, depth only</h3>
    <div class="ramp p2">
      <button class="swatch light-txt" style="background:#C24AC2" data-copy="#C24AC2"><span class="step">400</span><span>#C24AC2</span></button>
      <button class="swatch light-txt" style="background:#B000B0" data-copy="#B000B0"><span class="step">500</span><span>#B000B0</span></button>
      <button class="swatch light-txt" style="background:#8F008F" data-copy="#8F008F"><span class="step">600</span><span>#8F008F</span></button>
      <button class="swatch light-txt" style="background:#6B006B" data-copy="#6B006B"><span class="step">700</span><span>#6B006B</span></button>
    </div>
    <p class="ramp-note"><strong>#8F008F on the dark canvas is 1.8:1.</strong> Gradient stops and chart series only — never text on dark.</p>

    <h3 style="margin:24px 0 8px;">Neutrals &amp; surfaces</h3>
    <div class="grid g2">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Dark (default)</div>
        <div class="ramp p2" style="margin:0;">
          <div class="swatch light-txt" style="background:#1F2937" data-copy="#1F2937"><span class="step">base</span><span>#1F2937</span></div>
          <div class="swatch light-txt" style="background:#273244" data-copy="#273244"><span class="step">raised</span><span>#273244</span></div>
          <div class="swatch light-txt" style="background:#2F3A4D" data-copy="#2F3A4D"><span class="step">overlay</span><span>#2F3A4D</span></div>
          <div class="swatch light-txt" style="background:#161E29" data-copy="#161E29"><span class="step">sunken</span><span>#161E29</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Light (supported)</div>
        <div class="ramp p2" style="margin:0;">
          <div class="swatch dark-txt" style="background:#FFFFFF" data-copy="#FFFFFF"><span class="step">base</span><span>#FFFFFF</span></div>
          <div class="swatch dark-txt" style="background:#FAFAFC" data-copy="#FAFAFC"><span class="step">raised</span><span>#FAFAFC</span></div>
          <div class="swatch dark-txt" style="background:#F0F0F5" data-copy="#F0F0F5"><span class="step">overlay</span><span>#F0F0F5</span></div>
          <div class="swatch dark-txt" style="background:#F3F4F6" data-copy="#F3F4F6"><span class="step">sunken</span><span>#F3F4F6</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="ramp-note" style="margin-top:8px;">
      <strong>Opacity rule:</strong> hierarchy is built from <em>opacity of base-content</em>
      (70% secondary, 55% tertiary, 40% disabled) — never from a new grey. That is what keeps
      400+ components consistent across both themes.
    </p>

    <h3 style="margin:24px 0 8px;">Semantic — same hue, different lightness</h3>
    <div class="grid g4" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
      <div class="card"><span class="badge info">info</span><div class="mono" style="font-size:11px; color:var(--fg-3); margin-top:8px;">dark oklch(75% .22 220)<br>light #4696DC</div><p style="margin:6px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">Neutral information, links.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="badge success">success</span><div class="mono" style="font-size:11px; color:var(--fg-3); margin-top:8px;">dark oklch(68% .28 140)<br>light #3CB450</div><p style="margin:6px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">Saved, passed, merged, connected.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="badge warning">warning</span><div class="mono" style="font-size:11px; color:var(--fg-3); margin-top:8px;">dark oklch(82% .26 70)<br>light #FFB428</div><p style="margin:6px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">Budget, retry, degraded, review.</p></div>
      <div class="card"><span class="badge error">error</span><div class="mono" style="font-size:11px; color:var(--fg-3); margin-top:8px;">dark oklch(68% .32 25)<br>light #F05050</div><p style="margin:6px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">Failed, destructive, blocked.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="ramp-note">Magenta never means "error". Magenta means <em>codx-junior</em>.</p>

    <h3 style="margin:24px 0 8px;">Contrast — the numbers that constrain the design</h3>
    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Foreground</th><th>on #1F2937 (dark)</th><th>on #FFFFFF (light)</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>#CC0099 brand</td><td><span class="chip err">3.1 : 1 ✕</span></td><td><span class="chip ok">4.8 : 1 ✓</span></td><td>Fill on dark, text on light</td></tr>
          <tr><td>#FF69B4 pink</td><td><span class="chip ok">5.5 : 1 ✓</span></td><td><span class="chip err">2.0 : 1 ✕</span></td><td>Text on dark only</td></tr>
          <tr><td>#8F008F purple</td><td><span class="chip err">1.8 : 1 ✕</span></td><td><span class="chip ok">8.2 : 1 ✓</span></td><td>Gradient / fill on dark</td></tr>
          <tr><td>#FFFFFF on #CC0099</td><td><span class="chip ok">4.8 : 1 ✓</span></td><td>—</td><td>Primary buttons pass</td></tr>
          <tr><td>#FFFFFF on #FF69B4</td><td><span class="chip err">2.0 : 1 ✕</span></td><td>—</td><td>Pink fills need dark text</td></tr>
          <tr><td>#111827 on #FF69B4</td><td><span class="chip ok">10.4 : 1 ✓</span></td><td>—</td><td>Ink on pink passes</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g2">
      <div class="demo">
        <div class="demo-label">The 10% rule — correct</div>
        <div style="height:110px; border-radius:6px; background:var(--raised); border:1px solid var(--border-subtle); position:relative; overflow:hidden;">
          <div style="position:absolute; left:10px; top:10px; width:70px; height:22px; border-radius:4px; background:#CC0099;"></div>
          <div style="position:absolute; left:10px; top:44px; width:52px; height:8px; border-radius:3px; background:color-mix(in oklab, var(--fg) 12%, transparent);"></div>
          <div style="position:absolute; left:10px; top:60px; width:110px; height:8px; border-radius:3px; background:color-mix(in oklab, var(--fg) 8%, transparent);"></div>
          <div style="position:absolute; right:10px; top:10px; width:6px; height:6px; border-radius:50%; background:#CC0099;"></div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin:8px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">≈6% magenta: one primary action, one status dot.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="demo">
        <div class="demo-label">Lost hierarchy</div>
        <div style="height:110px; border-radius:6px; background:linear-gradient(120deg,#CC0099,#8F008F); position:relative; overflow:hidden;">
          <div style="position:absolute; left:10px; top:20px; width:130px; height:14px; border-radius:3px; background:rgba(255,255,255,.5);"></div>
          <div style="position:absolute; left:10px; top:44px; width:100px; height:10px; border-radius:3px; background:rgba(255,255,255,.35);"></div>
          <div style="position:absolute; left:10px; top:64px; width:60px; height:26px; border-radius:4px; background:#FF69B4;"></div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin:8px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">Nothing stands out — reduce the accent surface, don't add a colour.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ Typography ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="type">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">05</span><h2>Typography</h2></div>
    <p class="sub">Two voices. The interface speaks in a neutral system sans, the machine speaks in
      monospace. <strong>Test:</strong> if a user could paste the string into a terminal and it would mean
      something, it is monospace. That single rule makes the product read technical and calm.</p>

    <div class="grid g2" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
      <div class="demo">
        <div class="demo-label">Interface voice</div>
        <div style="font-size:16px; line-height:26px;">Save changes · Task Manager · Running tests… 3 of 12</div>
        <div class="mono" style="font-size:11px; color:var(--fg-3); margin-top:8px;">system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, "Noto Sans", sans-serif</div>
      </div>
      <div class="demo">
        <div class="demo-label">Machine voice</div>
        <div class="mono" style="font-size:16px; line-height:26px;">claude-sonnet-4-5 · api/chat/chat.py · 12.4k</div>
        <div class="mono" style="font-size:11px; color:var(--fg-3); margin-top:8px;">ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
      <div class="demo-label">Scale — eight steps</div>
      <div class="spec"><div class="t">display · 36/40 · 600</div><div class="t-display">Build faster, together</div></div>
      <div class="spec"><div class="t">h1 · 24/32 · 600</div><div class="t-h1">Task Manager</div></div>
      <div class="spec"><div class="t">h2 · 20/28 · 600</div><div class="t-h2">Sprint 12 · 14 tasks</div></div>
      <div class="spec"><div class="t">h3 · 16/24 · 600</div><div class="t-h3">Assignees</div></div>
      <div class="spec"><div class="t">body · 14/20 · 400</div><div class="t-body">Default UI text: table cells, buttons, sidebar labels, dense surfaces.</div></div>
      <div class="spec"><div class="t">body-lg · 16/26 · 400</div><div class="t-body-lg">Reading surfaces: chat prose, docs, settings descriptions.</div></div>
      <div class="spec"><div class="t">label · 12/16 · 500</div><div class="t-label">FORM LABEL · metadata · badges</div></div>
      <div class="spec"><div class="t">mono · 13/20</div><div class="t-mono">const tokens = read('design-tokens.json')</div></div>
      <div class="spec"><div class="t">code · 14/20</div><div class="t-code">diff --git a/client/src/main.ts b/client/src/main.ts</div></div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g2">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Weight &amp; numbers</div>
        <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--fg-2); margin-bottom:8px;">400 body · 500 labels and interactive text · 600 headings.
          <strong>Never 700+</strong> (system UI turns shouty), <strong>never 300</strong> on dark.</p>
        <table style="margin:0;">
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="num">12,482</td><td class="num">$0.42</td><td class="num">3m 12s</td><td class="num">1.2 GB</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <div class="mono" style="font-size:11px; color:var(--fg-3); margin-top:6px;">font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums — any column of numbers, always</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Measures</div>
        <table style="margin:0;">
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Chat message</td><td>62–78 ch (<code>max-width 800px</code>)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Docs / wiki</td><td><code>max-width: 68ch</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Tables &amp; logs</td><td>no limit — horizontal scroll, never wrap a hash</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Form group</td><td><code>max-width: 480px</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Modal body</td><td><code>max-width: 672px</code></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 style="margin:24px 0 8px;">Code typography</h3>
    <div class="codeblock">
      <div class="bar"><span class="file">client/src/assets/main.css — target</span>
        <button class="copybtn" data-copy=".view-code pre, .view-code code.hljs {
  font-family: var(--font-mono);
  font-size: 14px;          /* 16px is too large for side-by-side diffs */
  line-height: 20px;        /* absolute px — diffs align by pixel */
  letter-spacing: 0;
  font-feature-settings: &quot;liga&quot; 0, &quot;calt&quot; 0;
  tab-size: 2;
}">Copy</button></div>
      <pre><code><span class="k">.view-code</span> pre, <span class="k">.view-code</span> code.hljs {
  font-family: <span class="s">var(--font-mono)</span>;
  font-size: <span class="s">14px</span>;          <span class="c">/* 16px is too large for side-by-side diffs */</span>
  line-height: <span class="s">20px</span>;        <span class="c">/* absolute px — diffs align by pixel */</span>
  letter-spacing: <span class="s">0</span>;
  font-feature-settings: <span class="s">"liga" 0, "calt" 0</span>;  <span class="c">/* keep: no ligature confusion */</span>
  tab-size: <span class="s">2</span>;              <span class="c">/* add: 4 spaces breaks diff alignment */</span>
}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="pair">
      <div class="do"><div class="h">✓ Do</div><div class="body">Sentence case: <em>Save changes</em>, <em>12 files changed</em>, <em>3m 12s</em>, <em>codx-junior</em>.</div></div>
      <div class="dont"><div class="h">✕ Don't</div><div class="body"><em>Save Changes</em>, <em>12 file(s) changed</em>, <em>3 minutes and 12 seconds</em>, <em>CodxJunior</em>.</div></div>
    </div>
    <p class="ramp-note"><strong>Known bug:</strong> the <code>@font-face</code> in <code>main.css</code> points at a Google
      <em>stylesheet</em> URL, which can never be a font <code>src</code> — the face never loads. Delete it and use the
      system mono stack.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ Voice ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="voice">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">06</span><h2>Voice &amp; tone</h2></div>
    <p class="sub"><strong>An experienced teammate who happens to be a machine.</strong> Direct, specific,
      calm, honest about uncertainty, second person and active. Not a mascot, not a hype-man,
      not a helpdesk script.</p>

    <div class="tbl-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th style="width:150px;">Context</th><th style="width:180px;">Tone</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Empty state</td><td>Inviting, one action</td><td><strong>No chats yet.</strong> Start one and codx-junior will pick up your project context. <code>[New chat]</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Working</td><td>Terse, present continuous</td><td><code>Running tests… 3 of 12</code> · <code>Reading api/chat/chat_engine.py</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Success</td><td>One word, or one line + detail</td><td><code>Merged</code> · <code>PR #128 merged into main. 4 files changed.</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Warning</td><td>Factual + the threshold</td><td><code>Daily budget at 82%. Runs will pause at 100%.</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Error (recoverable)</td><td>What happened + what to do</td><td><strong>Couldn't reach the API.</strong> Check the container is running, then retry. <code>[Retry]</code> <code>[View logs]</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Destructive confirm</td><td>Consequence first, verb last</td><td><strong>Delete board "Sprint 12"?</strong> 14 tasks will be removed. This can't be undone. <code>[Cancel]</code> <code>[Delete board]</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>Handover to human</td><td>Explicit, no ambiguity</td><td><code>Waiting for you — login required.</code> <code>[Take over]</code></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g2" style="margin-bottom:16px;">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Error formula</div>
        <div class="codeblock" style="margin:0;"><pre><code>[What failed]. [Why, if known]. [What to do next].</code></pre></div>
        <ul style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px; color:var(--fg-2);">
          <li>Couldn't start the container. Port 8080 is already in use. Stop the other service or change the port.</li>
          <li>Git push rejected. The remote has 3 commits you don't have. Pull first, then push again.</li>
          <li>Request timed out after 120s. The model may be overloaded. Retry, or switch to a smaller model.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Use these words</div>
        <table style="margin:0; font-size:12px;">
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>chat</td><td>not conversation / thread / session</td></tr>
            <tr><td>task · board · column · card</td><td>not ticket / issue / lane</td></tr>
            <tr><td>run · step</td><td>not job / execution / phase</td></tr>
            <tr><td>profile · team</td><td>not persona / agent role / bot</td></tr>
            <tr><td>workspace</td><td>not sandbox / environment</td></tr>
            <tr><td>take over</td><td>not intervene / hijack</td></tr>
            <tr><td>budget · cxjcoins</td><td>not credits / quota / tokens</td></tr>
            <tr><td>knowledge</td><td>never RAG / embeddings in UI</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g3">
      <div class="demo"><div class="demo-label">Empty (first use)</div><div class="empty" style="padding:12px 0;"><div class="ic">◇</div><h4>No chats yet</h4><p>Start one and codx-junior will pick up your project context.</p><button class="btn btn-primary btn-sm">New chat</button></div></div>
      <div class="demo"><div class="demo-label">Empty (filtered) — never the first-use text</div><div class="empty" style="padding:12px 0;"><div class="ic">⌕</div><h4>No results for <code>auth</code></h4><p>Try a different term or clear the filters.</p><button class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm">Clear filters</button></div></div>
      <div class="demo"><div class="demo-label">Loading</div><div class="empty" style="padding:12px 0;"><div class="ic"><span class="spinner" style="border-color:color-mix(in oklab, var(--primary) 30%, transparent); border-top-color:var(--primary); width:22px; height:22px;"></span></div><h4>Starting codx-junior…</h4><p>Not "Wake up, codx-junior…" — that belongs on the landing page.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ Foundations ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="foundations">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="num">07</span><h2>Foundations</h2></div>
    <p class="sub">The primitives every component composes. This is the part that must not drift.</p>

    <div class="grid g2">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Spacing — 4px base, 8px rhythm</div>
        <div class="bars">
          <div class="bar-row"><span>0.5 · 2px</span><div class="b" style="width:2px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>1 · 4px</span><div class="b" style="width:4px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>1.5 · 6px</span><div class="b" style="width:6px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>2 · 8px</span><div class="b" style="width:8px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>3 · 12px</span><div class="b" style="width:12px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>4 · 16px</span><div class="b" style="width:16px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>5 · 20px</span><div class="b" style="width:20px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>6 · 24px</span><div class="b" style="width:24px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>8 · 32px</span><div class="b" style="width:32px"></div></div>
          <div class="bar-row"><span>12 · 48px</span><div class="b" style="width:48px"></div></div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">
          <strong>Rhythm:</strong> between siblings <code>2 / 3 / 4</code>; between regions <code>6 / 8</code>.
          Mixing the two is what makes dense UIs feel cramped <em>and</em> scattered.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Radius — three names are the contract</div>
        <div class="rgrid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);">
          <div class="rbox" style="border-radius:var(--radius-field);">field · 6px</div>
          <div class="rbox" style="border-radius:var(--radius-box);">box · 8px</div>
          <div class="rbox" style="border-radius:var(--radius-selector);">selector · 12px</div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">
          Inputs · cards, panels, dropdowns, toasts · tabs, nav items, <strong>dialogs</strong>.
          <code>radius.full</code> for pills, avatars, dots. <strong>Never mix radii inside one component.</strong>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="grid g2" style="margin-top:12px;">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="demo-label">Elevation — surface + border, not shadow</div>
        <div class="egrid">
          <div class="elayer e0">0 · flat — canvas / panel</div>
          <div class="elayer e1">1 · raised — card + border.subtle</div>
          <div class="elayer e2">2 · overlay — dropdown, toast + shadow-lg</div>
          <div class="elayer e3">3 · modal — dialog + shadow-2xl + backdrop blur</div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:12px; color:var(--fg-2);">Dark UIs cannot rely on shadows. No shadow on a flat surface, ever.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
